    "message": "fix(release): stamp the bundled compass with the release it ships in\n\nThe compass in the release tarball carries no version marker, so\ngetInstalledCompassVersion() reads 0.0.0 and `ix upgrade` treats a\ncompass it just shipped as \"not installed\" — then replaces it with\nwhatever ix-compass-dist has, which is older than a bundle built from\ncompass main at release time.\n\nv0.9.0 shipped exactly that. On Windows an unrelated tar failure masked\nit; everywhere else the swap succeeds and silently reverts the map to the\n2026-06-08 build, undoing the release. install.sh already writes this\nfile after extracting, so a fresh install was fine and only the upgrade\npath lost the stamp.\n\nThe Ix version rather than a compass version: the bundle is built from\ncompass main at release time, so it is always at least as new as any\nix-compass-dist release cut before it, which makes the Ix version a\nmonotonic stand-in. A genuine dist release published later at a higher\nnumber is still offered.\n\nBoth archive branches then verify the stamp is really inside the artifact\nrather than trusting tar and 7z to carry a dot-named file. Losing it\nproduces no error at all — every upgrade just quietly reverts the\ncompass — so it has to fail at the point of packaging or not at all.",
